  "data": {
    "body": " Consider the alternating series  $\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^{k+1}}{k }$\n\nWhich of the following statements is/are correct?\n\nI. The series converges absolutely\n\nII. The series converges because $\\lim _{k \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{1}{k}=0$ and $\\frac{1}{k}$ is always decreasing\n\nIII. The series diverges because $\\int_{1}^{\\infty}\\left|a_{k}(x)\\right| d x=\\int_{1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{x} d x$ diverges",
    "solution": [
      1
    ],
